Since this morning every single request fails. Our SDK retries for minutes and nothing gets through.

{"type":"error","error":{"type":"rate_limit_error","message":"You have reached your API usage limits: your organization has crossed its monthly API usage threshold, set based on your organization's API tier. You will regain access on 2026-11-01 at 00:00 UTC.","details":{"error_code":"enforced_spend_limit_reached"}},"request_id":"req_011CTS7bNwq2Vx8RfJ1mPz4K"}

There's no retry-after header on these.

I log in with my Max account but Claude Code says:

API Error: 401 {"type":"error","error":{"type":"authentication_error","message":"invalid x-api-key"},"request_id":"req_011CTT4mHq7Bc9Vx2NsR8wLd"}

I did set an API key months ago for a side project. Not sure if that matters.

Uploading a few large PDFs as base64 in one message fails with:

HTTP/1.1 413
{"type":"error","error":{"type":"request_too_large","message":"Request exceeds the maximum allowed number of bytes."},"request_id":"req_011CTU1xVb6Nq3Pz8KdW2rYm"}

